title: The Beer Hall Putsch
subtitle: Hitler proclaims a national revolution in Munich.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 11 and beer_hall_putsch = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
RG.news(Q.bavaria_soviet == 2 ? 'Hitler and Ludendorff cross into Red Bavaria and are beaten' : 'Hitler putsch fails at the Odeonsplatz', 3);
Q.beer_hall_putsch = 1;
if (Q.spd_in_government && Q.dvp_in_government && Q.e22_workers_gov == 0) {
    Q.spd_in_government = 0;
    Q.government_name = Q.government_name.replace(', SPD', '');
}
Q.e23_beer_in_crisis = Q.crisis_october ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.crisis_october) { Q.e23_oct_bonus += 1.5; }
!}

= The Beer Hall Putsch

[? if bavaria_soviet != 2 : On the evening of 8 November Adolf Hitler walks into the Bürgerbräukeller with a pistol while Kahr is speaking to three thousand guests. He fires into the ceiling and announces that the national revolution has begun. Ludendorff arrives an hour later in full uniform. The next morning two thousand men march on the War Ministry, and at the Odeonsplatz the Bavarian state police open fire. Hitler is arrested two days later at a villa by the Staffelsee. ?][? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : On the night of 8 November Hitler and Ludendorff lead the nationalist leagues over the Franconian border into Red Bavaria. The workers' guard is waiting at the Danube bridges. A squad of railwaymen takes Ludendorff prisoner, and Hitler gets back over the border in a borrowed car. ?]

[? if e23_beer_in_crisis = 1 : Seeckt now has a putsch behind him as well as our hundreds in front, and he has to send two regiments south. ?][? if e23_beer_in_crisis = 0 : Half the officer corps wanted Hitler to win, and most of them still hold their commands. ?]

- @strike: Call a one-day strike against the fascists.
- @front: Ask the SPD and the unions for joint defence squads.
- @trial: Publish who knew about the putsch.

@strike
subtitle: The works stop for a day. The emergency commanders will treat us like the putschists.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('bavaria', {militancy: 6});
RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 4, repression: 4});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Whole works stop in Berlin and the Ruhr. In Munich the strike committee is arrested by the same police who fired at the Odeonsplatz.

@front
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The SPD's members want it. Their executive may not.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e23_beer_front = Q.spd_relation >= 30 ? 1 : 0;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
if (Q.e23_beer_front) { Q.sa_strength *= 0.7; }
!}

[? if e23_beer_front = 1 : In thirty towns the Reichsbanner men and our hundreds patrol the same streets on the same nights. The brown shirts stay indoors. ?][? if e23_beer_front = 0 : The SPD executive refuses to sit with us. A few of its branches send men anyway. ?]

@trial
subtitle: Our informants in Munich have names. The officers named will not forget it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ledger('We printed the names of the officers who knew about the Munich putsch.', 'e23_trial');
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.army_loyalty -= 3;
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* prints the names of every Reichswehr officer in Bavaria who knew about the putsch in advance. The list runs to three columns, and two of the officers are retired within the month.
